PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L04U6.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":6,"theme":"Clever Inventions","essential_question":"How do inventions solve problems and change our lives?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1","title":"The Robot Moved Slowly: Adverbs of Manner","objectives":["Students will be able to form adverbs of manner from adjectives and use them after verbs.","Students will be able to compare actions with comparative adverbs (faster, more carefully, better).","I can say \"He worked carefully\" and \"She speaks English well.\"","I can say \"My robot moves faster than yours.\""],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين ظروف الحال من الصفات واستخدامها بعد الأفعال.","سيتمكن الطلاب من مقارنة الأفعال بظروف المقارنة.","أستطيع أن أقول He worked carefully وShe speaks English well.","أستطيع أن أقول My robot moves faster than yours."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"invent","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnt/","definition":"to make or design something new for the first time","arabic":"يخترع","example":"Who invented the telephone?","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-W01"},{"word":"inventor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛntɚ/","definition":"a person who invents things","arabic":"مخترع","example":"Al-Jazari was a famous Muslim inventor.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-W02"},{"word":"invention","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnʃən/","definition":"something new that someone has invented","arabic":"اختراع","example":"The light bulb was an important invention.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-W03"},{"word":"machine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/məˈʃin/","definition":"a thing with moving parts that does work","arabic":"آلة","example":"A washing machine saves a lot of time.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Adjectives describe nouns (a slow robot). Adverbs of manner describe how we do an action (The robot moved slowly).\nMost adverbs = adjective + -ly: quick → quickly, careful → carefully. Spelling: happy → happily, gentle → gently, automatic → automatically. Irregular: good → well, fast → fast, hard → hard, late → late.\nAdverbs usually come after the verb or after the object: She speaks English well (NOT She speaks well English). Comparatives: faster, harder, better, more carefully, more quietly.\nadjective + ly: slow → slowly, careful → carefully\ny → ily: easy → easily; le → ly: gentle → gently; ic → ically: automatic → automatically\nirregular: good → well • fast → fast • hard → hard • late → late\ncomparative: faster, harder, better, more slowly, more carefully","examples":["The baby slept peacefully.","Please close the door quietly.","My grandpa speaks slowly and clearly.","Rakan runs very fast.","She did well in the science test.","The new car moves more quietly than the old one.","Our team played better in the second half.","The lights turn on automatically at night."],"common_errors":["✗ He speaks English very good. → ✓ He speaks English very well. (good → well (adverb).)","✗ She drives careful. → ✓ She drives carefully. (Describe the verb → adverb.)","✗ He speaks fluently English. → ✓ He speaks English fluently. (Adverb after the object.)","✗ The robot moved more fast. → ✓ The robot moved faster. (fast → faster.)"],"arabic":"الصفة تصف الاسم (a slow robot)، وظرف الحال يصف كيف يتم الفعل (The robot moved slowly).\nنضيف ly للصفة: careful → carefully، وy تصبح ily: happy → happily.\nصيغ شاذة: good → well، وfast وhard وlate لا تتغير.\nالظرف يأتي بعد الفعل أو بعد المفعول: She speaks English well (وليس speaks well English)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Robot Moved Slowly: Adverbs of Manner”. Let’s learn adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U6-LS1 | The Robot Moved Slowly: Adverbs of Manner","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Adam's Robot”: Adam loves inventions. Last month, he built a small robot for the school science fair. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Adam loves inventions. Last month, he built a small robot for the school science fair.","visual":"Image GV-L04-U6-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Adjectives describe nouns (a slow robot). Adverbs of manner describe how we do an action (The robot moved slowly). Most adverbs = adjective + -ly: quick → quickly, careful → carefully. Spelling: happy → happily, gentle → gently, automatic → automatically. Irregular: good → well, fast → fast, hard → hard, late → late.","on_screen":"adjective + ly: slow → slowly, careful → carefully • y → ily: easy → easily; le → ly: gentle → gently; ic → ically: automatic → automatically • irregular: good → well • fast → fast • hard → hard • late → late","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The baby slept peacefully. Please close the door quietly. My grandpa speaks slowly and clearly.","on_screen":"The baby slept peacefully. / Please close the door quietly. / My grandpa speaks slowly and clearly.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He speaks English very good.” That’s not right. We say: “He speaks English very well.” good → well (adverb).","on_screen":"✗ He speaks English very good.   ✓ He speaks English very well.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"He drives carefully.\" Does \"carefully\" describe \"he\" or \"drives\"? … Think! … *drives* – how he drives. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"He worked carefully\" and \"She speaks English well.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"He worked carefully\" and \"She speaks English well.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الصفة تصف الاسم (a slow robot)، وظرف الحال يصف كيف يتم الفعل (The robot moved slowly).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He speaks English very good. — الصحيح: He speaks English very well.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول He worked carefully وShe speaks English well."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Adam's Robot","body":"Adam loves inventions. Last month, he built a small robot for the school science fair.\nHe worked carefully every evening, and his dad helped him patiently.\nAt first, the robot moved slowly, and it couldn't climb stairs. Adam wanted it to move faster, so he added a stronger battery.\nOn the day of the fair, the robot worked perfectly! It picked up trash quickly and put it in a bin.\nThe judges watched closely because the invention was useful and clever.\nAdam won second prize, and he smiled happily all day.\nNext year, he wants to design a robot that can water plants automatically.","word_count":104,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The old man walked ___.","options":["more slow","slowlier","slowly","slow"],"answer":"slowly","explanation":"Adjective + -ly = adverb of manner.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + ly = ظرف."},{"q":"Please write your name ___.","options":["clearly","clearer","clear","clearness"],"answer":"clearly","explanation":"Adjective + -ly = adverb of manner.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + ly = ظرف."},{"q":"The children played ___ in the garden.","options":["happyly","happily","happy","happier"],"answer":"happily","explanation":"y → ily; le → ly; ic → ically.","explanation_ar":"تغييرات التهجئة."},{"q":"My cousin speaks English very ___.","options":["well","goodly","good","better than"],"answer":"well","explanation":"good → well; fast, hard, late don't change.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"The cheetah runs ___.","options":["more fast","fastly","fastest of","fast"],"answer":"fast","explanation":"good → well; fast, hard, late don't change.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"She is a ___ driver.","options":["caringly","careful","carefully","care"],"answer":"careful","explanation":"Adjective describes a noun; adverb describes a verb.","explanation_ar":"الصفة للاسم والظرف للفعل."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the adverb. Word bank: gently, easily, automatically","items":[{"q":"The robot opened the door ______ (automatic).","options":[],"answer":"automatically","explanation":"y → ily; le → ly; ic → ically.","explanation_ar":"تغييرات التهجئة."},{"q":"The nurse held the baby ______ (gentle).","options":[],"answer":"gently","explanation":"y → ily; le → ly; ic → ically.","explanation_ar":"تغييرات التهجئة."},{"q":"We finished the puzzle ______ (easy).","options":[],"answer":"easily","explanation":"y → ily; le → ly; ic → ically.","explanation_ar":"تغييرات التهجئة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-B2","type":"order","instructions":"Guided practice: Put the words in order.","items":[{"q":"English / She / speaks / fluently   ( . )","options":["English","She","speaks","fluently"],"answer":"She speaks English fluently.","explanation":"Word order: The adverb goes after the verb or the object.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: مكان الظرف."},{"q":"My / brother / well / football / plays   ( . )","options":["My","brother","well","football","plays"],"answer":"My brother plays football well.","explanation":"Word order: good → well; fast, hard, late don't change.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"The / students / hard / very / worked   ( . )","options":["The","students","hard","very","worked"],"answer":"The students worked very hard.","explanation":"Word order: good → well; fast, hard, late don't change.","explanation_ar":"ترتيب الكلمات: صيغ شاذة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about how people do things.","items":[{"q":"My mom cooks ___.","options":[],"answer":"My mom cooks very well.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My best friend runs ___.","options":[],"answer":"My best friend runs fast.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"In the library, we must speak ___.","options":[],"answer":"In the library, we must speak quietly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I do my homework ___.","options":[],"answer":"I do my homework carefully.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Compare two people: ___ swims faster than ___.","options":[],"answer":"Saad swims faster than Ali.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Describe an invention in action.","items":[{"q":"Choose a machine (a washing machine, a drone, a robot vacuum). Write 3 sentences with adverbs.","options":[],"answer":"The robot vacuum moves slowly. It cleans the floor carefully. It turns automatically at the wall.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Compare two machines with comparative adverbs.","options":[],"answer":"An electric car moves more quietly than a gas car. A plane travels faster than a train.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with an adjective and one with its adverb.","options":[],"answer":"Faisal is a quick runner. Faisal runs quickly.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Ball Toss Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Students stand in a circle. The teacher says a cue word and throws the ball.","The catcher makes a sentence with the cue word and adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster).","If it is correct, the catcher chooses the next cue word and throws the ball to a new student.","If it is not correct, classmates help fix it, and the same student tries again."],"data":[{"label":"slowly"},{"label":"quickly"},{"label":"carefully"},{"label":"quietly"},{"label":"happily"},{"label":"well"},{"label":"fast"},{"label":"hard"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The teacher explained the lesson ___.","options":["clear","clearer","clearly","clearness"],"answer":"clearly","explanation":"Adjective + -ly = adverb of manner.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + ly = ظرف."},{"q":"The bird sang ___ in the morning.","options":["beautifull","beautifully","beautifuly","beautiful"],"answer":"beautifully","explanation":"Adjective + -ly = adverb of manner.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + ly = ظرف."},{"q":"The baby is sleeping ___.","options":["peaceful","peace","peacefuly","peacefully"],"answer":"peacefully","explanation":"Adjective + -ly = adverb of manner.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + ly = ظرف."},{"q":"","options":["My dad drives carefuly.","My dad drives careful.","My dad carefully drives careful.","My dad drives carefully."],"answer":"My dad drives carefully.","explanation":"Adjective + -ly = adverb of manner.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + ly = ظرف."},{"q":"","options":["You did very well on the test!","You did very goodly on the test!","You did very good on the test!","You did very best on the test!"],"answer":"You did very well on the test!","explanation":"good → well; fast, hard, late don't change.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"","options":["He speaks Arabic and English perfectly.","He perfect speaks Arabic and English.","He speaks Arabic and English perfect.","He speaks perfectly Arabic and English."],"answer":"He speaks Arabic and English perfectly.","explanation":"The adverb goes after the verb or the object.","explanation_ar":"مكان الظرف."},{"q":"My brother works ___. He never stops.","options":["hardy","more hardly","hardly","hard"],"answer":"hard","explanation":"good → well; fast, hard, late don't change.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"Can you speak ___, please? I don't understand.","options":["slowest","more slowly","slowlier","more slow"],"answer":"more slowly","explanation":"Comparative adverbs: faster, better, more carefully.","explanation_ar":"مقارنة الظروف."},{"q":"The new robot works ___ than the old one.","options":["more good","gooder","better","more well"],"answer":"better","explanation":"Comparative adverbs: faster, better, more carefully.","explanation_ar":"مقارنة الظروف."},{"q":"","options":["She is a quiet girl. She talks quiet.","She is a quiet girl. She talks quietly.","She is a quietly girl. She talks quiet.","She is quietly girl. She talks quietly."],"answer":"She is a quiet girl. She talks quietly.","explanation":"Adjective describes a noun; adverb describes a verb.","explanation_ar":"الصفة للاسم والظرف للفعل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"A school science fair: Adam's small robot picking up trash and putting it in a bin while judges with clipboards watch closely and Adam smiles. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A school science fair: Adam's small robot picking up trash and putting it in a bin while judges with clipboards watch closely and Adam smiles"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about adverbs of manner (-ly"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows invent (to make or design something new for the first time); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing invent: to make or design something new for the first time"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows inventor (a person who invents things); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing inventor: a person who invents things"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows invention (something new that someone has invented); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing invention: something new that someone has invented"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows machine (a thing with moving parts that does work); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing machine: a thing with moving parts that does work"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Ball Toss Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Ball Toss Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-W01","script":"invent. invent. Who invented the telephone?","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-W02","script":"inventor. inventor. Al-Jazari was a famous Muslim inventor.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-W03","script":"invention. invention. The light bulb was an important invention.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-W04","script":"machine. machine. A washing machine saves a lot of time.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-T1","script":"Adam loves inventions. Last month, he built a small robot for the school science fair. He worked carefully every evening, and his dad helped him patiently. At first, the robot moved slowly, and it couldn't climb stairs. Adam wanted it to move faster, so he added a stronger battery. On the day of the fair, the robot worked perfectly! It picked up trash quickly and put it in a bin. The judges watched closely because the invention was useful and clever. Adam won second prize, and he smiled happily all day. Next year, he wants to design a robot that can water plants automatically.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Robot Moved Slowly: Adverbs of Manner”. Let’s learn adverbs of manner (-ly; well, fast, hard) and comparative adverbs (more carefully, faster) together. Listen to the start of “Adam's Robot”: Adam loves inventions. Last month, he built a small robot for the school science fair. Look at the green words. Adjectives describe nouns (a slow robot). Adverbs of manner describe how we do an action (The robot moved slowly). Most adverbs = adjective + -ly: quick → quickly, careful → carefully. Spelling: happy → happily, gentle → gently, automatic → automatically. Irregular: good → well, fast → fast, hard → hard, late → late. Here are some examples. The baby slept peacefully. Please close the door quietly. My grandpa speaks slowly and clearly. Be careful! Some learners say: “He speaks English very good.” That’s not right. We say: “He speaks English very well.” good → well (adverb). Quick check: \"He drives carefully.\" Does \"carefully\" describe \"he\" or \"drives\"? … Think! … *drives* – how he drives. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"He worked carefully\" and \"She speaks English well.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2","title":"The Robot Is Small, but It Is Strong: and, but, or, so, because","objectives":["Students will be able to join ideas with and (add), but (contrast), or (choice), so (result) and because (reason).","Students will be able to choose the conjunction that shows the right meaning.","I can join two ideas with and, but or or.","I can explain reasons and results with because and so."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من ربط الأفكار بـ and (إضافة) وbut (تضاد) وor (اختيار) وso (نتيجة) وbecause (سبب).","سيتمكن الطلاب من اختيار أداة الربط التي تعبّر عن المعنى الصحيح.","أستطيع أن أربط فكرتين بـ and أو but أو or.","أستطيع أن أشرح الأسباب والنتائج بـ because وso."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"robot","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈroʊˌbɑt/","definition":"a machine that can do jobs automatically","arabic":"روبوت","example":"The robot cleaned the floor by itself.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-W01"},{"word":"battery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbætɚi/","definition":"a thing that gives electricity to small machines","arabic":"بطارية","example":"My phone battery is almost empty.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-W02"},{"word":"engine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛndʒən/","definition":"the part of a car or plane that makes it move","arabic":"محرك","example":"The car's engine is very quiet.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-W03"},{"word":"screen","pos":"noun","ipa":"/skrin/","definition":"the flat glass part of a TV, phone or computer","arabic":"شاشة","example":"Don't touch the screen with wet hands.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Conjunctions join words or sentences. and adds information: The robot is small and light.\nbut shows a contrast (a different idea): The robot is small, but it is strong. or gives a choice: Do you want tea or juice?\nso shows a result: The battery was dead, so the car stopped. because shows a reason: The car stopped because the battery was dead.","examples":["Adam built a robot and a remote control.","The machine is old, but it still works.","Do you want to use a pencil or a pen?","My phone was broken, so I used my dad's phone.","We stayed inside because it was very hot.","Electric cars are quiet and clean.","The invention was clever, but it was too expensive.","You can take the bus or walk to the museum."],"common_errors":["✗ I was tired so I went to bed because. → ✓ I was tired, so I went to bed. (Use one conjunction for the result.)","✗ Because it was raining. (alone) → ✓ We stayed inside because it was raining. (A because-clause needs a main clause.)","✗ The car is fast but it is new. → ✓ The car is fast and it is new. (Two positive ideas → and, not but.)","✗ I didn't go because I was sick so. → ✓ I didn't go because I was sick. (Don't add so at the end.)"],"arabic":"أدوات الربط: and للإضافة، وbut للتضاد، وor للاختيار، وso للنتيجة، وbecause للسبب.\nThe battery was dead, so the car stopped (نتيجة) / The car stopped because the battery was dead (سبب).\nجملة because وحدها ليست جملة كاملة، يجب أن تتصل بجملة رئيسة."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Robot Is Small, but It Is Strong: and, but, or, so, because”. Let’s learn conjunctions and, but, or, so, because together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U6-LS2 | The Robot Is Small, but It Is Strong: and, but, or, so, because","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: I like robots, so I joined the robotics club. • He won because he practiced every day. It isn't expensive, but it isn't very useful. Do you want to build a robot or a car? • Why did it stop? – Because the battery was empty.","on_screen":"I like robots, so I joined the robotics club. • He won because he practiced every day. | It isn't expensive, but it isn't very useful. | Do you want to build a robot or a car? • Why did it stop? – Because the battery was empty.","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Conjunctions join words or sentences. and adds information: The robot is small and light. but shows a contrast (a different idea): The robot is small, but it is strong. or gives a choice: Do you want tea or juice?","on_screen":"conjunctions and, but, or, so, because","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Adam built a robot and a remote control. The machine is old, but it still works. Do you want to use a pencil or a pen?","on_screen":"Adam built a robot and a remote control. / The machine is old, but it still works. / Do you want to use a pencil or a pen?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “I was tired so I went to bed because.” That’s not right. We say: “I was tired, so I went to bed.” Use one conjunction for the result.","on_screen":"✗ I was tired so I went to bed because.   ✓ I was tired, so I went to bed.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"It was late, so we went home.\" Which part is the result? … Think! … we went home. Great job! Now you can say: I can join two ideas with and, but or or.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can join two ideas with and, but or or.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: conjunctions and, but, or, so, because.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","أدوات الربط: and للإضافة، وbut للتضاد، وor للاختيار، وso للنتيجة، وbecause للسبب.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: I was tired so I went to bed because. — الصحيح: I was tired, so I went to bed.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أربط فكرتين بـ and أو but أو or."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct conjunction.","items":[{"q":"The robot is small, ___ it is very strong.","options":["so","but","or","and"],"answer":"but","explanation":"but = a contrast (different idea).","explanation_ar":"but للتضاد."},{"q":"Would you like water ___ juice?","options":["and","so","or","but"],"answer":"or","explanation":"or = a choice.","explanation_ar":"or للاختيار."},{"q":"It was raining, ___ we stayed home.","options":["because","or","so","but"],"answer":"so","explanation":"so = a result.","explanation_ar":"so للنتيجة."},{"q":"The car stopped ___ it had no gas.","options":["because","or","and","so"],"answer":"because","explanation":"because = a reason.","explanation_ar":"because للسبب."},{"q":"My brother likes robots ___ computers.","options":["but","so","or","and"],"answer":"and","explanation":"and = add another idea.","explanation_ar":"and للإضافة."},{"q":"The phone is new, ___ the battery doesn't last long.","options":["but","so","or","and"],"answer":"but","explanation":"but = a contrast (different idea).","explanation_ar":"but للتضاد."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Join the sentences with the word in brackets.","items":[{"q":"The machine is useful.  +  It saves time. (and)","options":[],"answer":"The machine is useful, and it saves time.","explanation":"and = add another idea.","explanation_ar":"and للإضافة."},{"q":"I wanted to buy the drone.  +  It was too expensive. (but)","options":[],"answer":"I wanted to buy the drone, but it was too expensive.","explanation":"but = a contrast (different idea).","explanation_ar":"but للتضاد."},{"q":"The battery was empty.  +  The toy didn't work. (so)","options":[],"answer":"The battery was empty, so the toy didn't work.","explanation":"so = a result.","explanation_ar":"so للنتيجة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-B2","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write so or because. Word bank: so, because","items":[{"q":"Lina is happy ______ she won the science prize.","options":[],"answer":"because","explanation":"because = a reason.","explanation_ar":"because للسبب."},{"q":"The road was closed, ______ we took a different way.","options":[],"answer":"so","explanation":"so = a result.","explanation_ar":"so للنتيجة."},{"q":"The lights went out ______ there was a storm.","options":[],"answer":"because","explanation":"because = a reason.","explanation_ar":"because للسبب."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Complete the sentences about you.","items":[{"q":"I like science because ___.","options":[],"answer":"I like science because experiments are fun.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses conjunctions and, but, or, so, because correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I was tired yesterday, so ___.","options":[],"answer":"I was tired yesterday, so I went to bed early.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses conjunctions and, but, or, so, because correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"I want to be an inventor, but ___.","options":[],"answer":"I want to be an inventor, but I need to study hard first.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses conjunctions and, but, or, so, because correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"After school, I can play football or ___.","options":[],"answer":"After school, I can play football or read a book.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses conjunctions and, but, or, so, because correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My favorite machine is ___ because ___.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite machine is the airplane because it can fly anywhere.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses conjunctions and, but, or, so, because correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Problem and solution.","items":[{"q":"Write 2 sentences about a problem and a solution with so.","options":[],"answer":"My little brother is often bored, so I made him a puzzle.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses conjunctions and, but, or, so, because correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences explaining why an invention is useful with because.","options":[],"answer":"The washing machine is useful because it saves time. Phones are useful because we can call anyone.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses conjunctions and, but, or, so, because correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with but about an invention that has a problem.","options":[],"answer":"Cars are fast, but they make a lot of pollution.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses conjunctions and, but, or, so, because correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Dice Sentences","mechanic":"spin_wheel","rules":["Turn over a cue card and roll the die.","Make a sentence with the cue in the form shown by the die.","The player on the left checks; a correct sentence wins the card.","The player with the most cards after 7 minutes wins."],"data":[{"cue":"I like robots / I want to build one / so"},{"cue":"the robot is small / it is strong / but"},{"cue":"do you want tea / juice / or"},{"cue":"he won / he worked hard / because"},{"cue":"the battery was dead / the car stopped / so"},{"cue":"she studies / she plays chess / and"},{"cue":"it is old / it still works / but"},{"cue":"we can walk / we can take the bus / or"},{"cue":"I was late / the bus broke down / because"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The drone is fast, ___ it is very noisy.","options":["or","but","so","and"],"answer":"but","explanation":"but = a contrast (different idea).","explanation_ar":"but للتضاد."},{"q":"Do you want to make a robot ___ a rocket?","options":["but","and","or","so"],"answer":"or","explanation":"or = a choice.","explanation_ar":"or للاختيار."},{"q":"I forgot my charger, ___ my phone died.","options":["or","so","but","because"],"answer":"so","explanation":"so = a result.","explanation_ar":"so للنتيجة."},{"q":"We need a new fridge ___ the old one is broken.","options":["because","or","so","and"],"answer":"because","explanation":"because = a reason.","explanation_ar":"because للسبب."},{"q":"","options":["The camera is small so light.","The camera is small but light and.","The camera is small or light.","The camera is small and light."],"answer":"The camera is small and light.","explanation":"and = add another idea.","explanation_ar":"and للإضافة."},{"q":"","options":["Because it was Friday.","The museum was closed because it was Friday so.","The museum was closed so it was Friday.","The museum was closed because it was Friday."],"answer":"The museum was closed because it was Friday.","explanation":"because = a reason.","explanation_ar":"because للسبب."},{"q":"Which conjunction shows a result?","options":["so","because","but","or"],"answer":"so","explanation":"so = a result.","explanation_ar":"so للنتيجة."},{"q":"","options":["He studied hard, because he passed the test.","He studied hard so because he passed the test.","He studied hard, so he passed the test.","He studied hard, or he passed the test."],"answer":"He studied hard, so he passed the test.","explanation":"so = a result.","explanation_ar":"so للنتيجة."},{"q":"The invention was clever, ___ nobody bought it.","options":["and","but","because","so"],"answer":"but","explanation":"but = a contrast (different idea).","explanation_ar":"but للتضاد."},{"q":"You can call me ___ send me a message.","options":["so","because","or","but"],"answer":"or","explanation":"or = a choice.","explanation_ar":"or للاختيار."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Five puzzle pieces connecting two halves of sentences, each piece labeled with a conjunction and a small icon (+, ↔, ?, →, ←). Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Five puzzle pieces connecting two halves of sentences, each piece labeled with a conjunction and a small icon (+, ↔, ?, →, ←)"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of conjunctions and, but, or, so, because: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Clever Inventions”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of conjunctions and, but, or, so, because: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Clever Inventions”"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows robot (a machine that can do jobs automatically); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing robot: a machine that can do jobs automatically"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows battery (a thing that gives electricity to small machines); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing battery: a thing that gives electricity to small machines"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows engine (the part of a car or plane that makes it move); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing engine: the part of a car or plane that makes it move"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows screen (the flat glass part of a TV, phone or computer); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing screen: the flat glass part of a TV, phone or computer"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Dice Sentences”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Dice Sentences"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-W01","script":"robot. robot. The robot cleaned the floor by itself.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-W02","script":"battery. battery. My phone battery is almost empty.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-W03","script":"engine. engine. The car's engine is very quiet.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-W04","script":"screen. screen. Don't touch the screen with wet hands.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Robot Is Small, but It Is Strong: and, but, or, so, because”. Let’s learn conjunctions and, but, or, so, because together. Remember these patterns: I like robots, so I joined the robotics club. • He won because he practiced every day. It isn't expensive, but it isn't very useful. Do you want to build a robot or a car? • Why did it stop? – Because the battery was empty. Conjunctions join words or sentences. and adds information: The robot is small and light. but shows a contrast (a different idea): The robot is small, but it is strong. or gives a choice: Do you want tea or juice? Here are some examples. Adam built a robot and a remote control. The machine is old, but it still works. Do you want to use a pencil or a pen? Be careful! Some learners say: “I was tired so I went to bed because.” That’s not right. We say: “I was tired, so I went to bed.” Use one conjunction for the result. Quick check: \"It was late, so we went home.\" Which part is the result? … Think! … we went home. Great job! Now you can say: I can join two ideas with and, but or or.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3","title":"Inventors and Designers: Words with -er and -or","objectives":["Students will be able to use words about inventions and machines.","Students will be able to make nouns for people with -er and -or.","I can talk about inventions and machines.","I can make words like \"inventor\" and \"designer\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام كلمات الاختراعات والآلات.","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين أسماء الأشخاص بإضافة er أو or.","أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الاختراعات والآلات.","أستطيع أن أكوّن كلمات مثل inventor وdesigner."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"design","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/dɪˈzaɪn/","definition":"to plan how something will look and work; the plan","arabic":"يصمم / تصميم","example":"She designed a new kind of chair.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W01"},{"word":"solve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/sɑlv/","definition":"to find an answer to a problem","arabic":"يحل","example":"This app solves a big problem for farmers.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W02"},{"word":"useful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈjusfəl/","definition":"helping you to do something","arabic":"مفيد","example":"A compass is useful in the desert.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W03"},{"word":"electric","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪˈlɛktrɪk/","definition":"using electricity to work","arabic":"كهربائي","example":"Electric cars don't use gasoline.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W04"},{"word":"automatically","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˌɔtəˈmætɪkli/","definition":"by itself, without a person controlling it","arabic":"تلقائيًا","example":"The doors open automatically.","image_id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"Invention words: invent (verb) → invention (thing) → inventor (person). Others: machine, robot, battery, engine, screen, electric, useful, solve a problem.\nAdd -er or -or to a verb to make a noun for the person who does it: design → designer, build → builder, invent → inventor, visit → visitor, act → actor.\nSpelling: if the verb ends in e, add only -r: drive → driver, manage → manager. Some nouns double the consonant: run → runner.\nWord families: invent: inventor (n), invention (n), inventive (adj) | design: designer (n), design (n) | create: creator (n), creation (n), creative (adj) | operate: operator (n), operation (n) | use: user (n), useful (adj), useless (adj)\nCollocations/phrases: solve a problem • invent a machine • charge a battery • start the engine • touch the screen • design a product","examples":["Al-Jazari was a great Muslim inventor.","His elephant clock was a clever invention.","The designer drew the new car on a computer.","The builders finished the bridge in one year.","Visitors can try the robots at the science center.","You must charge the battery every night.","The drone operator controlled it from the ground.","This app solves a big problem for farmers."],"common_errors":["✗ He is a good inventer. → ✓ He is a good inventor. (invent → inventor (-or).)","✗ The design of the car is a famous designor. → ✓ The designer of the car is famous. (design → designer (-er).)","✗ The invent of the telephone changed the world. → ✓ The invention of the telephone changed the world. (Use the noun invention.)","✗ A drive must be careful. → ✓ A driver must be careful. (Person → driver.)"],"arabic":"invent (يخترع) ← invention (اختراع) ← inventor (مخترع).\nنضيف er أو or للفعل لنحصل على اسم الشخص: design → designer وvisit → visitor.\nإذا انتهى الفعل بـ e نضيف r فقط: drive → driver.\nالجزري عالم ومخترع مسلم مشهور، ومن اختراعاته ساعة الفيل."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Inventors and Designers: Words with -er and -or”. Let’s learn invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U6-LS3 | Inventors and Designers: Words with -er and -or","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. design: to plan how something will look and work; the plan. solve: to find an answer to a problem. useful: helping you to do something.","on_screen":"design | solve | useful","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Invention words: invent (verb) → invention (thing) → inventor (person). Others: machine, robot, battery, engine, screen, electric, useful, solve a problem. Add -er or -or to a verb to make a noun for the person who does it: design → designer, build → builder, invent → inventor, visit → visitor, act → actor.","on_screen":"invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor)","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Al-Jazari was a great Muslim inventor. His elephant clock was a clever invention. The designer drew the new car on a computer.","on_screen":"Al-Jazari was a great Muslim inventor. / His elephant clock was a clever invention. / The designer drew the new car on a computer.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “He is a good inventer.” That’s not right. We say: “He is a good inventor.” invent → inventor (-or).","on_screen":"✗ He is a good inventer.   ✓ He is a good inventor.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: What do we call a person who designs things? … Think! … A *designer*. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about inventions and machines.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can talk about inventions and machines.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","invent (يخترع) ← invention (اختراع) ← inventor (مخترع).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: He is a good inventer. — الصحيح: He is a good inventor.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أتحدث عن الاختراعات والآلات."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"A person who invents things is an ___.","options":["inventor","inventive","invention","inventer"],"answer":"inventor","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"A person who visits a museum is a ___.","options":["visiting","visitor","visiter","visit"],"answer":"visitor","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"The ___ of the airplane changed travel forever.","options":["invent","inventor","inventive","invention"],"answer":"invention","explanation":"Choose the word-family member (verb, noun, person).","explanation_ar":"فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"My phone is dead. I need to charge the ___.","options":["screen","robot","battery","engine"],"answer":"battery","explanation":"Use the right invention collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The car won't move. There's a problem with the ___.","options":["engine","battery charger","screen","inventor"],"answer":"engine","explanation":"Choose the machine word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الآلة المناسبة."},{"q":"A person who designs clothes is a ___.","options":["designing","design","designer","designor"],"answer":"designer","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the verb to the person.","items":[{"q":"build","options":["builder","operator","creator","driver","actor","teacher"],"answer":"builder","explanation":"build → builder. Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"act","options":["builder","operator","creator","driver","actor","teacher"],"answer":"actor","explanation":"act → actor. Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"drive","options":["builder","operator","creator","driver","actor","teacher"],"answer":"driver","explanation":"drive → driver. Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"operate","options":["builder","operator","creator","driver","actor","teacher"],"answer":"operator","explanation":"operate → operator. Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"teach","options":["builder","operator","creator","driver","actor","teacher"],"answer":"teacher","explanation":"teach → teacher. Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"create","options":["builder","operator","creator","driver","actor","teacher"],"answer":"creator","explanation":"create → creator. Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about inventions.","items":[{"q":"The most useful invention in my house is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The most useful invention in my house is the fridge.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"An inventor I know about is ___.","options":[],"answer":"An inventor I know about is Al-Jazari.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A machine that solves a problem for my family is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A machine that solves a problem for my family is the dishwasher.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"When I grow up, I want to be a ___ (-er/-or word).","options":[],"answer":"When I grow up, I want to be a designer.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Something electric that I use every day is ___.","options":[],"answer":"Something electric that I use every day is my tablet.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Design an invention.","items":[{"q":"Draw an invention that solves a problem. Name it and write what it does.","options":[],"answer":"The Smart Bag: it reminds you of your books automatically.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 sentences about who will use it and why it is useful.","options":[],"answer":"Students will use it. It is useful because they won't forget books. Teachers will be happy too.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 3 -er/-or words about people who will make or use your invention.","options":[],"answer":"designer, builder, user","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Vocabulary Bingo","mechanic":"matching","rules":["Students write nine words from the list in their grid.","The teacher (or a student caller) reads a definition or Arabic meaning.","Students cross out the matching word.","Three in a row = \"Bingo!\" The winner must read the words and say what each means."],"data":[{"word":"invent","match":"to make or design something new for the first time","arabic":"يخترع"},{"word":"inventor","match":"a person who invents things","arabic":"مخترع"},{"word":"invention","match":"something new that someone has invented","arabic":"اختراع"},{"word":"machine","match":"a thing with moving parts that does work","arabic":"آلة"},{"word":"robot","match":"a machine that can do jobs automatically","arabic":"روبوت"},{"word":"battery","match":"a thing that gives electricity to small machines","arabic":"بطارية"},{"word":"engine","match":"the part of a car or plane that makes it move","arabic":"محرك"},{"word":"screen","match":"the flat glass part of a TV, phone or computer","arabic":"شاشة"},{"word":"design","match":"to plan how something will look and work; the plan","arabic":"يصمم / تصميم"},{"word":"solve","match":"to find an answer to a problem","arabic":"يحل"},{"word":"useful","match":"helping you to do something","arabic":"مفيد"},{"word":"electric","match":"using electricity to work","arabic":"كهربائي"},{"word":"automatically","match":"by itself, without a person controlling it","arabic":"تلقائيًا"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The ___ of the new bridge are working day and night.","options":["builds","buildors","building","builders"],"answer":"builders","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"Al-Jazari ___ many clever machines.","options":["inventor","inventive","invention","invented"],"answer":"invented","explanation":"Choose the word-family member (verb, noun, person).","explanation_ar":"فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"A person who acts in films is an ___.","options":["acting","actor","acter","act"],"answer":"actor","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"You must ___ the battery before you use the drone.","options":["charge","touch","solve","start"],"answer":"charge","explanation":"Use the right invention collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The flat glass part of a phone is the ___.","options":["battery","button","screen","engine"],"answer":"screen","explanation":"Choose the machine word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الآلة المناسبة."},{"q":"A person who drives a bus is a bus ___.","options":["driving","drivor","driver","drive"],"answer":"driver","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"The new app ___ a problem for drivers.","options":["designs out","solves","charges","invents"],"answer":"solves","explanation":"Use the right invention collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"The noun from \"create\" is ___ (the thing).","options":["creation","creative","creating","creator"],"answer":"creation","explanation":"Choose the word-family member (verb, noun, person).","explanation_ar":"فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"Cars that run on electricity are ___ cars.","options":["electricity","electrical-ly","electric","electrician"],"answer":"electric","explanation":"Choose the machine word that fits.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الآلة المناسبة."},{"q":"Which word is a person?","options":["operating","operation","operate","operator"],"answer":"operator","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A museum of inventions with exhibits: Al-Jazari's elephant water clock, a light bulb, a telephone, an electric car and a robot, with labels for inventor and designer. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A museum of inventions with exhibits: Al-Jazari's elephant water clock, a light bulb, a telephone, an electric car and a robot, with labels for inventor and designer"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows design (to plan how something will look and work; the plan); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing design: to plan how something will look and work; the plan"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows solve (to find an answer to a problem); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing solve: to find an answer to a problem"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows useful (helping you to do something); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing useful: helping you to do something"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows electric (using electricity to work); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing electric: using electricity to work"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows automatically (by itself, without a person controlling it); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing automatically: by itself, without a person controlling it"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Vocabulary Bingo”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Vocabulary Bingo"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W01","script":"design. design. She designed a new kind of chair.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W02","script":"solve. solve. This app solves a big problem for farmers.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W03","script":"useful. useful. A compass is useful in the desert.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W04","script":"electric. electric. Electric cars don't use gasoline.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-W05","script":"automatically. automatically. The doors open automatically.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Inventors and Designers: Words with -er and -or”. Let’s learn invention vocabulary; people nouns with the suffixes -er and -or (inventor, designer, visitor) together. Meet some new words. design: to plan how something will look and work; the plan. solve: to find an answer to a problem. useful: helping you to do something. Invention words: invent (verb) → invention (thing) → inventor (person). Others: machine, robot, battery, engine, screen, electric, useful, solve a problem. Add -er or -or to a verb to make a noun for the person who does it: design → designer, build → builder, invent → inventor, visit → visitor, act → actor. Here are some examples. Al-Jazari was a great Muslim inventor. His elephant clock was a clever invention. The designer drew the new car on a computer. Be careful! Some learners say: “He is a good inventer.” That’s not right. We say: “He is a good inventor.” invent → inventor (-or). Quick check: What do we call a person who designs things? … Think! … A *designer*. Great job! Now you can say: I can talk about inventions and machines.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS4","title":"The Robot Was Small, but It Was Strong: Commas in Compound Sentences","objectives":["Students will be able to join two complete sentences with a comma and and, but, or or so.","Students will be able to tell a compound sentence from a sentence that doesn't need a comma.","I can write \"The robot was small, but it was strong.\"","I can tell when I need a comma before and/but/so."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من ربط جملتين كاملتين بفاصلة وand أو but أو or أو so.","سيتمكن الطلاب من التمييز بين الجملة المركبة والجملة التي لا تحتاج إلى فاصلة.","أستطيع أن أكتب The robot was small, but it was strong.","أستطيع أن أعرف متى أحتاج إلى فاصلة قبل and/but/so."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"invent","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnt/","definition":"to make or design something new for the first time","arabic":"يخترع","example":"Who invented the telephone?","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"inventor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛntɚ/","definition":"a person who invents things","arabic":"مخترع","example":"Al-Jazari was a famous Muslim inventor.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"invention","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnʃən/","definition":"something new that someone has invented","arabic":"اختراع","example":"The light bulb was an important invention.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"machine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/məˈʃin/","definition":"a thing with moving parts that does work","arabic":"آلة","example":"A washing machine saves a lot of time.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"robot","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈroʊˌbɑt/","definition":"a machine that can do jobs automatically","arabic":"روبوت","example":"The robot cleaned the floor by itself.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"battery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbætɚi/","definition":"a thing that gives electricity to small machines","arabic":"بطارية","example":"My phone battery is almost empty.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"A compound sentence joins two complete sentences (each with a subject and a verb). Put a comma before the conjunction: The robot was small, but it was strong.\nThe conjunctions: and, but, or, so (also for, nor, yet – the \"FANBOYS\"). Example: The battery died, so the car stopped.\nDon't use a comma when and joins only two words or two verbs with the same subject: Adam built and tested the robot (one subject – no comma). Don't use a comma before because: The car stopped because the battery died.\nsentence + , + and/but/or/so + sentence\nEach part must have its own subject and verb.\nSame subject + two verbs → no comma: She designed and built it.\nNo comma before because (in the middle of a sentence).","examples":["The machine is old, but it works well.","I charged the battery, and the drone flew again.","You can use the robot, or you can clean by hand.","The screen was broken, so we bought a new tablet.","Adam designed and built the robot.","The lights went out because there was a storm.","My brother likes engines, and my sister likes computers.","The invention was useful, but it was very expensive."],"common_errors":["✗ The robot was small but it was strong. → ✓ The robot was small, but it was strong. (Two sentences → comma before but.)","✗ Adam designed, and built the robot. → ✓ Adam designed and built the robot. (Same subject, two verbs → no comma.)","✗ The car stopped, because the battery died. → ✓ The car stopped because the battery died. (No comma before because.)","✗ It rained, we stayed home. → ✓ It rained, so we stayed home. (A comma alone can't join two sentences – add a conjunction.)"],"arabic":"الجملة المركبة تربط جملتين كاملتين، ونضع فاصلة قبل and أو but أو or أو so.\nإذا كان الفاعل واحدًا مع فعلين فلا نضع فاصلة: Adam designed and built the robot.\nلا نضع فاصلة قبل because في وسط الجملة.\nالفاصلة وحدها لا تربط جملتين؛ نحتاج أداة ربط."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Robot Was Small, but It Was Strong: Commas in Compound Sentences”. Let’s learn compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U6-LS4 | The Robot Was Small, but It Was Strong: Commas in Compound Sentences","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"A compound sentence joins two complete sentences (each with a subject and a verb). Put a comma before the conjunction: The robot was small, but it was strong.","on_screen":"compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"A compound sentence joins two complete sentences (each with a subject and a verb). Put a comma before the conjunction: The robot was small, but it was strong. The conjunctions: and, but, or, so (also for, nor, yet – the \"FANBOYS\"). Example: The battery died, so the car stopped.","on_screen":"sentence + , + and/but/or/so + sentence • Each part must have its own subject and verb. • Same subject + two verbs → no comma: She designed and built it.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The machine is old, but it works well. I charged the battery, and the drone flew again. You can use the robot, or you can clean by hand.","on_screen":"The machine is old, but it works well. / I charged the battery, and the drone flew again. / You can use the robot, or you can clean by hand.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The robot was small but it was strong.” That’s not right. We say: “The robot was small, but it was strong.” Two sentences → comma before but.","on_screen":"✗ The robot was small but it was strong.   ✓ The robot was small, but it was strong.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"She likes robots and she builds them.\" Two sentences? Do we need a comma? … Think! … Yes – She likes robots, and she builds them. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The robot was small, but it was strong.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write \"The robot was small, but it was strong.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","الجملة المركبة تربط جملتين كاملتين، ونضع فاصلة قبل and أو but أو or أو so.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The robot was small but it was strong. — الصحيح: The robot was small, but it was strong.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب The robot was small, but it was strong."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"The Solar Fan (editing passage)","body":"Lina wanted a cool room so she designed a solar fan. She found an old motor and her dad gave her a small solar panel. She built, and tested the fan in two days. The fan was quiet but it wasn't very strong. She worked hard, because she wanted to win.","word_count":51,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct sentence.","items":[{"q":"","options":["The drone is small but it can fly high,","The drone, is small but it can fly high.","The drone is small but, it can fly high.","The drone is small, but it can fly high."],"answer":"The drone is small, but it can fly high.","explanation":"Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"","options":["Sara designed and painted the poster.","Sara, designed and painted the poster.","Sara designed, and painted the poster.","Sara designed and, painted the poster."],"answer":"Sara designed and painted the poster.","explanation":"Same subject + two verbs → no comma.","explanation_ar":"فاعل واحد وفعلان ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["The bus was late, because there was traffic.","The bus was late because there was traffic.","The bus, was late because there was traffic.","The bus was late because, there was traffic."],"answer":"The bus was late because there was traffic.","explanation":"No comma before because.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل because."},{"q":"","options":["The battery was low, I charged it.","The battery, was low so I charged it.","The battery was low, so I charged it.","The battery was low so, I charged it."],"answer":"The battery was low, so I charged it.","explanation":"A comma alone can't join two sentences.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة وحدها لا تربط جملتين."},{"q":"","options":["You can build a car or you can, build a plane.","You can build a car or, you can build a plane.","You can build a car, or you can build a plane.","You can, build a car or you can build a plane."],"answer":"You can build a car, or you can build a plane.","explanation":"Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"","options":["The engine, started and the car moved.","The engine started and, the car moved.","The engine started, the car moved and.","The engine started, and the car moved."],"answer":"The engine started, and the car moved.","explanation":"Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Add or remove a comma.","items":[{"q":"The robot is clever and it can talk.","options":[],"answer":"The robot is clever, and it can talk.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"My dad fixed, and cleaned the old radio.","options":[],"answer":"My dad fixed and cleaned the old radio.","explanation":", → (delete). Same subject + two verbs → no comma.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). فاعل واحد وفعلان ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"The screen is bright but the sound is quiet.","options":[],"answer":"The screen is bright, but the sound is quiet.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"We stayed inside, because it was too hot.","options":[],"answer":"We stayed inside because it was too hot.","explanation":", → (delete). No comma before because.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). لا فاصلة قبل because."},{"q":"The fridge was broken so the food went bad.","options":[],"answer":"The fridge was broken, so the food went bad.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"I wanted to watch TV but the power was off.","options":[],"answer":"I wanted to watch TV, but the power was off.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the invention report.","items":[{"q":"Lina wanted a cool room so she designed a solar fan.","options":[],"answer":"Lina wanted a cool room, so she designed a solar fan.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"Lina wanted a cool room so she designed a solar fan.","options":[],"answer":"Lina wanted a cool room, so she designed a solar fan.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"She built, and tested the fan in two days.","options":[],"answer":"She built and tested the fan in two days.","explanation":", → (delete). Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"Lina wanted a cool room so she designed a solar fan.","options":[],"answer":"Lina wanted a cool room, so she designed a solar fan.","explanation":"(add) → ,. Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: (add) → ,. جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"She built, and tested the fan in two days.","options":[],"answer":"She built and tested the fan in two days.","explanation":", → (delete). Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: , → (delete). جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write compound sentences.","items":[{"q":"Write one compound sentence with but about a machine.","options":[],"answer":"My phone is old, but it still works.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one compound sentence with so about a problem.","options":[],"answer":"The printer was out of ink, so I couldn't print my homework.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with the same subject and two verbs (no comma).","options":[],"answer":"My brother opened and fixed the toy car.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Letter Ladder","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["The leader chooses a word from the list and draws one blank line per letter.","Teams take turns guessing letters. Correct letters are written on the lines.","Each wrong guess removes one rung of the ladder (start with 6 rungs).","The team that completes the word scores 2 points and uses it in a sentence."],"data":[{"word":"invent","clue":"to make or design something new for the first time"},{"word":"inventor","clue":"a person who invents things"},{"word":"invention","clue":"something new that someone has invented"},{"word":"machine","clue":"a thing with moving parts that does work"},{"word":"battery","clue":"a thing that gives electricity to small machines"},{"word":"automatically","clue":"by itself, without a person controlling it"},{"word":"robot","clue":"a machine that can do jobs automatically"},{"word":"engine","clue":"the part of a car or plane that makes it move"},{"word":"screen","clue":"the flat glass part of a TV, phone or computer"},{"word":"design","clue":"to plan how something will look and work; the plan"},{"word":"solve","clue":"to find an answer to a problem"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["The car is electric and it doesn't make, noise.","The car is electric, and it doesn't make noise.","The car, is electric and it doesn't make noise.","The car is electric and, it doesn't make noise."],"answer":"The car is electric, and it doesn't make noise.","explanation":"Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"The lamp is old but it still works.\"","options":["after \"but\"","after \"lamp\"","after \"works\"","before \"but\""],"answer":"before \"but\"","explanation":"Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"","options":["Omar opened and read the instructions.","Omar opened, and read the instructions.","Omar opened and, read the instructions.","Omar, opened and read the instructions."],"answer":"Omar opened and read the instructions.","explanation":"Same subject + two verbs → no comma.","explanation_ar":"فاعل واحد وفعلان ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["I couldn't call you, because my phone was dead.","I couldn't call you because, my phone was dead.","I couldn't, call you because my phone was dead.","I couldn't call you because my phone was dead."],"answer":"I couldn't call you because my phone was dead.","explanation":"No comma before because.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل because."},{"q":"Choose the compound sentence that is missing its comma.","options":["The robot stopped because it was tired.","The robot is small and light.","The robot moved and stopped.","The robot moved slowly but it didn't stop."],"answer":"The robot moved slowly but it didn't stop.","explanation":"Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"","options":["It was dark so, I turned on the flashlight.","It was dark, so I turned on the flashlight.","It was dark, I turned on the flashlight.","It was, dark so I turned on the flashlight."],"answer":"It was dark, so I turned on the flashlight.","explanation":"A comma alone can't join two sentences.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة وحدها لا تربط جملتين."},{"q":"","options":["Do you want to watch the video, or do you want to read the book?","Do you want to watch the video or, do you want to read the book?","Do you want to watch the video or do you want, to read the book?","Do you want to watch, the video or do you want to read the book?"],"answer":"Do you want to watch the video, or do you want to read the book?","explanation":"Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."},{"q":"","options":["The inventor drew and tested, his idea.","The inventor drew, and tested his idea.","The inventor drew and tested his idea.","The inventor, drew and tested his idea."],"answer":"The inventor drew and tested his idea.","explanation":"Same subject + two verbs → no comma.","explanation_ar":"فاعل واحد وفعلان ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"What is wrong? \"The battery died, the drone fell.\"","options":["Nothing is wrong.","It needs a comma before \"died\".","It needs a conjunction after the comma.","It needs \"because\" at the end."],"answer":"It needs a conjunction after the comma.","explanation":"A comma alone can't join two sentences.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة وحدها لا تربط جملتين."},{"q":"","options":["The screen cracked, but the phone still worked.","The screen cracked but, the phone still worked.","The screen, cracked but the phone still worked.","The screen cracked but the phone still, worked."],"answer":"The screen cracked, but the phone still worked.","explanation":"Two complete sentences → comma before and/but/or/so.","explanation_ar":"جملتان كاملتان ← فاصلة قبل أداة الربط."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Clever Inventions” that shows compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Clever Inventions” that shows compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences in action"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Letter Ladder”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Letter Ladder"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Robot Was Small, but It Was Strong: Commas in Compound Sentences”. Let’s learn compound sentences: comma before and, but, or, so when joining two complete sentences together. A compound sentence joins two complete sentences (each with a subject and a verb). Put a comma before the conjunction: The robot was small, but it was strong. A compound sentence joins two complete sentences (each with a subject and a verb). Put a comma before the conjunction: The robot was small, but it was strong. The conjunctions: and, but, or, so (also for, nor, yet – the \"FANBOYS\"). Example: The battery died, so the car stopped. Here are some examples. The machine is old, but it works well. I charged the battery, and the drone flew again. You can use the robot, or you can clean by hand. Be careful! Some learners say: “The robot was small but it was strong.” That’s not right. We say: “The robot was small, but it was strong.” Two sentences → comma before but. Quick check: \"She likes robots and she builds them.\" Two sentences? Do we need a comma? … Think! … Yes – She likes robots, and she builds them. Great job! Now you can say: I can write \"The robot was small, but it was strong.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS5","title":"Pitch Your Invention: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to present an invention idea and explain how it works and why it is useful.","Students will be able to write an invention pitch with adverbs, conjunctions and correctly punctuated compound sentences.","I can present my invention idea.","I can write an invention pitch."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من عرض فكرة اختراع وشرح طريقة عمله وفائدته.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة عرض لاختراع مع الظروف وأدوات الربط والجمل المركبة المرقّمة صحيحًا.","أستطيع أن أعرض فكرة اختراعي.","أستطيع أن أكتب عرضًا لاختراعي."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"invent","pos":"verb","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnt/","definition":"to make or design something new for the first time","arabic":"يخترع","example":"Who invented the telephone?","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"inventor","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛntɚ/","definition":"a person who invents things","arabic":"مخترع","example":"Al-Jazari was a famous Muslim inventor.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"invention","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˌɪnˈvɛnʃən/","definition":"something new that someone has invented","arabic":"اختراع","example":"The light bulb was an important invention.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"machine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/məˈʃin/","definition":"a thing with moving parts that does work","arabic":"آلة","example":"A washing machine saves a lot of time.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"robot","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈroʊˌbɑt/","definition":"a machine that can do jobs automatically","arabic":"روبوت","example":"The robot cleaned the floor by itself.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"battery","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈbætɚi/","definition":"a thing that gives electricity to small machines","arabic":"بطارية","example":"My phone battery is almost empty.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"engine","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈɛndʒən/","definition":"the part of a car or plane that makes it move","arabic":"محرك","example":"The car's engine is very quiet.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"screen","pos":"noun","ipa":"/skrin/","definition":"the flat glass part of a TV, phone or computer","arabic":"شاشة","example":"Don't touch the screen with wet hands.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"design","pos":"verb / noun","ipa":"/dɪˈzaɪn/","definition":"to plan how something will look and work; the plan","arabic":"يصمم / تصميم","example":"She designed a new kind of chair.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"solve","pos":"verb","ipa":"/sɑlv/","definition":"to find an answer to a problem","arabic":"يحل","example":"This app solves a big problem for farmers.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"useful","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈjusfəl/","definition":"helping you to do something","arabic":"مفيد","example":"A compass is useful in the desert.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"electric","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ɪˈlɛktrɪk/","definition":"using electricity to work","arabic":"كهربائي","example":"Electric cars don't use gasoline.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"automatically","pos":"adverb","ipa":"/ˌɔtəˈmætɪkli/","definition":"by itself, without a person controlling it","arabic":"تلقائيًا","example":"The doors open automatically.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 6: adverbs of manner, and/but/or/so/because, invention words, -er/-or nouns and commas in compound sentences.\nA pitch is a short talk or text that tries to make people like your idea. It says the problem, the solution, how it works and why it's good.\n✔ adverbs: gently, quietly, automatically, quickly\n✔ so (result), because (reason), but (contrast)\n✔ comma before and/but/so/or in compound sentences\n✔ invention words and -er/-or people","examples":["The bag reminds you automatically.","It works quietly, and it doesn't use much power.","Students forget their books, so we invented the Smart Bag.","It's useful because it saves time.","It's small, but it's very strong.","The designer tested it carefully.","You can charge it with a cable, or you can use the sun.","Every user will find it easily."],"common_errors":["✗ It works quiet. → ✓ It works quietly. (Describe the verb → adverb.)","✗ It is cheap but it is strong. (two positive ideas) → ✓ It is cheap, and it is strong. (Two positive ideas → and.)","✗ It's useful, because it saves time. → ✓ It's useful because it saves time. (No comma before because.)"],"arabic":"نراجع الظروف وأدوات الربط وكلمات الاختراع والجمل المركبة.\nالعرض (pitch) يذكر المشكلة والحل وطريقة العمل والفائدة.\nتذكّر الفاصلة قبل and/but/so عند ربط جملتين، ولا فاصلة قبل because."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Pitch Your Invention: Language in Use”. Let’s learn adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U6-LS5 | Pitch Your Invention: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Invention pitch: in teams, invent something that solves a school or home problem. Present it in 1 minute: what it is, how it works (adverbs), why it's useful (because/so) and one problem it still has (but).","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 6: adverbs of manner, and/but/or/so/because, invention words, -er/-or nouns and commas in compound sentences. A pitch is a short talk or text that tries to make people like your idea. It says the problem, the solution, how it works and why it's good.","on_screen":"✔ adverbs: gently, quietly, automatically, quickly • ✔ so (result), because (reason), but (contrast) • ✔ comma before and/but/so/or in compound sentences","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The bag reminds you automatically. It works quietly, and it doesn't use much power. Students forget their books, so we invented the Smart Bag.","on_screen":"The bag reminds you automatically. / It works quietly, and it doesn't use much power. / Students forget their books, so we invented the Smart Bag.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “It works quiet.” That’s not right. We say: “It works quietly.” Describe the verb → adverb.","on_screen":"✗ It works quiet.   ✓ It works quietly.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “It is cheap but it is strong. (two positive ideas)”? … Think! … It should be “It is cheap, and it is strong.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present my invention idea.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can present my invention idea.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع الظروف وأدوات الربط وكلمات الاختراع والجمل المركبة.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: It works quiet. — الصحيح: It works quietly.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعرض فكرة اختراعي."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Smart Water Bottle – Noura","body":"Many students forget to drink water, so I designed the Smart Water Bottle.\nThe bottle lights up gently every hour, and it plays a quiet sound.\nIt also measures how much you drink automatically.\nThe bottle is useful because it keeps students healthy and active.\nIt is a little expensive, but the battery lasts for a month.\nI think every user will love it!","word_count":64,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Noura's pitch. True or False?","items":[{"q":"Noura designed the bottle because students forget to drink water.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Smart Water Bottle – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The bottle lights up loudly every minute.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Smart Water Bottle – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"It measures how much you drink automatically.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Smart Water Bottle – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Noura says the bottle keeps students healthy.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Smart Water Bottle – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The bottle is very cheap.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Smart Water Bottle – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The battery lasts for a month.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Smart Water Bottle – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The bottle lights up ___ every hour.","options":["gentle","gentler","gentlely","gently"],"answer":"gently","explanation":"Adverb of manner (-ly).","explanation_ar":"ظرف الحال."},{"q":"Students forget to drink water, ___ Noura designed the bottle.","options":["because","but","so","or"],"answer":"so","explanation":"Choose the conjunction with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"أداة الربط المناسبة."},{"q":"It's useful ___ it keeps students healthy.","options":["but","or","so","because"],"answer":"because","explanation":"Choose the conjunction with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"أداة الربط المناسبة."},{"q":"A person who uses the bottle is a ___.","options":["usage","user","useful","usor"],"answer":"user","explanation":"Invention word or -er/-or person.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الاختراع."},{"q":"","options":["It's a little expensive, but the battery lasts long.","It's a little expensive, the battery lasts long.","It's, a little expensive but the battery lasts long.","It's a little expensive but, the battery lasts long."],"answer":"It's a little expensive, but the battery lasts long.","explanation":"Comma before and/but/so/or in a compound sentence.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة في الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"","options":["It's useful because, it reminds you.","It's useful, because it reminds you.","It's useful because it reminds you.","It's, useful because it reminds you."],"answer":"It's useful because it reminds you.","explanation":"No comma before because.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل because."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Invention pitch. Write your team's ideas.","items":[{"q":"Our invention is called ___.","options":[],"answer":"Our invention is called the Shoe Finder.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The problem: ___.","options":[],"answer":"People lose their shoes at the mosque.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"How it works (2 adverbs): ___","options":[],"answer":"It beeps quietly, and it lights up brightly when you call it.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Why it's useful (because): ___","options":[],"answer":"It's useful because it saves time.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"One problem (but): ___","options":[],"answer":"It's clever, but it needs a small battery.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your invention pitch.","items":[{"q":"Plan: name, problem, how it works, why useful, one problem.","options":[],"answer":"Homework Helper Lamp; students study in the dark; turns on automatically, reads aloud slowly; useful because it helps eyes; but it is big","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write your pitch in 6–7 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Many students study in bad light, so we invented the Homework Helper Lamp. It turns on automatically when you open a book. It reads difficult words slowly and clearly. The lamp is useful because it protects your eyes. It is big, but it fits on any desk. Every student will love it!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: adverbs? conjunctions? commas in compound sentences? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"It turns on automatic\" to \"It turns on automatically\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Treasure Hunt Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["Teams move to a station every 90 seconds.","At each station, write one correct sentence with the cue word and adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review).","Teams collect a \"treasure letter\" for each correct sentence.","Unscramble the letters at the end to reveal the secret word."],"data":[{"cue":"invent","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"inventor","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"invention","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"machine","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"robot","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"battery","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"engine","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"screen","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"design","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"solve","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"useful","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"electric","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"automatically","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The robot cleaned the room ___.","options":["perfect","perfectlly","more perfect","perfectly"],"answer":"perfectly","explanation":"Adverb of manner (-ly).","explanation_ar":"ظرف الحال."},{"q":"The fan is quiet, ___ it is very strong.","options":["so","but","because","and"],"answer":"and","explanation":"Choose the conjunction with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"أداة الربط المناسبة."},{"q":"I lost my keys, ___ I couldn't open the door.","options":["but","so","because","or"],"answer":"so","explanation":"Choose the conjunction with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"أداة الربط المناسبة."},{"q":"The ___ of the game was only twelve years old!","options":["creative","create","creator","creation"],"answer":"creator","explanation":"Invention word or -er/-or person.","explanation_ar":"كلمة الاختراع."},{"q":"","options":["The drone is light, it flies easily.","The drone, is light so it flies easily.","The drone is light so, it flies easily.","The drone is light, so it flies easily."],"answer":"The drone is light, so it flies easily.","explanation":"Comma before and/but/so/or in a compound sentence.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة في الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"","options":["We bought a fan because the room was hot.","We bought a fan because, the room was hot.","We bought a fan, because the room was hot.","We, bought a fan because the room was hot."],"answer":"We bought a fan because the room was hot.","explanation":"No comma before because.","explanation_ar":"لا فاصلة قبل because."},{"q":"She speaks very ___ on the phone. I can't hear her.","options":["quietly","quietlly","quiet","quieter than"],"answer":"quietly","explanation":"Adverb of manner (-ly).","explanation_ar":"ظرف الحال."},{"q":"Do you want the red model ___ the blue model?","options":["so","or","but","and"],"answer":"or","explanation":"Choose the conjunction with the right meaning.","explanation_ar":"أداة الربط المناسبة."},{"q":"","options":["The inventor worked hardly, and the machine was ready in a week.","The inventor worked hard and, the machine was ready in a week.","The inventor worked hard, and the machine was ready in a week.","The inventor, worked hard and the machine was ready in a week."],"answer":"The inventor worked hard, and the machine was ready in a week.","explanation":"Comma before and/but/so/or in a compound sentence.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة في الجملة المركبة."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for an invention pitch:","options":["Our robot works quietly, and it saves families a lot of time.","Our robot works quietly and, it saves families a lot of time.","Our robot work quietly, but it saves families a lot of time.","Our robot works quiet, and it saves families a lot of time."],"answer":"Our robot works quietly, and it saves families a lot of time.","explanation":"Adverb of manner (-ly).","explanation_ar":"ظرف الحال."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Noura presenting a cardboard model of a \"Smart Water Bottle\" to a panel of classmate judges, with a poster showing how it works. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Noura presenting a cardboard model of a \"Smart Water Bottle\" to a panel of classmate judges, with a poster showing how it works"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Clever Inventions”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Clever Inventions”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L04-U6-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Treasure Hunt Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Treasure Hunt Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS5-T1","script":"Many students forget to drink water, so I designed the Smart Water Bottle. The bottle lights up gently every hour, and it plays a quiet sound. It also measures how much you drink automatically. The bottle is useful because it keeps students healthy and active. It is a little expensive, but the battery lasts for a month. I think every user will love it!","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U6-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Pitch Your Invention: Language in Use”. Let’s learn adverbs of manner, conjunctions, invention words and compound sentences (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Invention pitch: in teams, invent something that solves a school or home problem. Present it in 1 minute: what it is, how it works (adverbs), why it's useful (because/so) and one problem it still has (but). Today you use all of Unit 6: adverbs of manner, and/but/or/so/because, invention words, -er/-or nouns and commas in compound sentences. A pitch is a short talk or text that tries to make people like your idea. It says the problem, the solution, how it works and why it's good. Here are some examples. The bag reminds you automatically. It works quietly, and it doesn't use much power. Students forget their books, so we invented the Smart Bag. Be careful! Some learners say: “It works quiet.” That’s not right. We say: “It works quietly.” Describe the verb → adverb. Quick check: what is wrong with “It is cheap but it is strong. (two positive ideas)”? … Think! … It should be “It is cheap, and it is strong.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present my invention idea.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"The turtle moved ___ across the sand.","options":["slow","slowly","more slow","slowlly"],"answer":"slowly","explanation":"Adjective + -ly = adverb of manner.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + ly = ظرف."},{"q":"The children waited ___ for the show to start.","options":["patiently","patience","patiently more","patient"],"answer":"patiently","explanation":"Adjective + -ly = adverb of manner.","explanation_ar":"الصفة + ly = ظرف."},{"q":"We won the match ___.","options":["easyly","easy","easier","easily"],"answer":"easily","explanation":"y → ily; le → ly; ic → ically.","explanation_ar":"تغييرات التهجئة."},{"q":"My uncle plays chess very ___.","options":["good","best","goodly","well"],"answer":"well","explanation":"good → well; fast, hard, late don't change.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"","options":["She speaks fluently French.","She speaks French fluently.","She fluent speaks French.","She speaks French fluent."],"answer":"She speaks French fluently.","explanation":"The adverb goes after the verb or the object.","explanation_ar":"مكان الظرف."},{"q":"Can you walk ___? I can't keep up!","options":["more slow","slowlier","more slowly","slowest"],"answer":"more slowly","explanation":"Comparative adverbs: faster, better, more carefully.","explanation_ar":"مقارنة الظروف."},{"q":"The lamp is old, ___ it still works.","options":["and","but","so","or"],"answer":"but","explanation":"but = a contrast (different idea).","explanation_ar":"but للتضاد."},{"q":"Would you like to build a robot ___ a car?","options":["or","so","but","and"],"answer":"or","explanation":"or = a choice.","explanation_ar":"or للاختيار."},{"q":"The fridge was broken, ___ the milk went bad.","options":["because","but","or","so"],"answer":"so","explanation":"so = a result.","explanation_ar":"so للنتيجة."},{"q":"I'm tired ___ I slept late.","options":["so","because","and","or"],"answer":"because","explanation":"because = a reason.","explanation_ar":"because للسبب."},{"q":"The person who invents things is an ___.","options":["inventor","inventive","inventer","invention"],"answer":"inventor","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"The ___ of the printing press changed the world.","options":["invent","inventive","inventor","invention"],"answer":"invention","explanation":"Choose the word-family member (verb, noun, person).","explanation_ar":"فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"You can't use the drone until you ___ the battery.","options":["start","charge","solve","touch"],"answer":"charge","explanation":"Use the right invention collocation.","explanation_ar":"المتلازمة الصحيحة."},{"q":"A person who visits a place is a ___.","options":["visitor","visit","visiting","visiter"],"answer":"visitor","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"The doors of the mall open ___.","options":["automatic","automation","automatically","automaticly"],"answer":"automatically","explanation":"y → ily; le → ly; ic → ically.","explanation_ar":"تغييرات التهجئة."},{"q":"Find the word for a person.","options":["designer","design","designed","designing"],"answer":"designer","explanation":"Verb + -er/-or = the person who does it.","explanation_ar":"الفعل + er/or = الشخص."},{"q":"","options":["The phone, is new but the battery is weak.","The phone is new but, the battery is weak.","The phone is new, the battery is weak.","The phone is new, but the battery is weak."],"answer":"The phone is new, but the battery is weak.","explanation":"Comparative adverbs: faster, better, more carefully.","explanation_ar":"مقارنة الظروف."},{"q":"","options":["My brother washed, and dried the dishes.","My brother washed and dried, the dishes.","My brother washed and dried the dishes.","My brother, washed and dried the dishes."],"answer":"My brother washed and dried the dishes.","explanation":"Same subject + two verbs → no comma.","explanation_ar":"فاعل واحد وفعلان ← بلا فاصلة."},{"q":"","options":["The match, stopped because it started to rain.","The match stopped because it started to rain.","The match stopped because, it started to rain.","The match stopped, because it started to rain."],"answer":"The match stopped because it started to rain.","explanation":"because = a reason.","explanation_ar":"because للسبب."},{"q":"What is wrong? \"The power went out, we lit candles.\"","options":["It needs \"because\" after \"candles\".","It needs a comma after \"we\".","It needs a conjunction after the comma.","Nothing is wrong."],"answer":"It needs a conjunction after the comma.","explanation":"A comma alone can't join two sentences.","explanation_ar":"الفاصلة وحدها لا تربط جملتين."},{"q":"Where does the comma go? \"The machine is heavy but it is easy to move.\"","options":["after \"but\"","after \"easy\"","after \"machine\"","before \"but\""],"answer":"before \"but\"","explanation":"Comparative adverbs: faster, better, more carefully.","explanation_ar":"مقارنة الظروف."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for an invention report:","options":["The robot moves quickly, and it can climb stairs.","The robot move quickly, but it can climb stairs.","The robot moves quickly and, it can climb stairs.","The robot moves quick, and it can climb stairs."],"answer":"The robot moves quickly, and it can climb stairs.","explanation":"Comparative adverbs: faster, better, more carefully.","explanation_ar":"مقارنة الظروف."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"the car is fast but it is very quiet\"","options":["The car is fast, so it is very quiet.","The car is fast but it is very quiet.","The car is fast, and it is very quiet.","the car is fast, and it is very quiet."],"answer":"The car is fast, and it is very quiet.","explanation":"and = add another idea.","explanation_ar":"and للإضافة."},{"q":"Why is the invention useful? – ___","options":["Because it saves water so.","It's useful, because it saves water.","It's useful because it saves water.","It's useful so it saves water."],"answer":"It's useful because it saves water.","explanation":"because = a reason.","explanation_ar":"because للسبب."}],"theme_ar":"اختراعات ذكية","essential_question_ar":"كيف تحل الاختراعات المشكلات وتغيّر حياتنا؟","can_do":"I can describe how things are done with adverbs, join ideas with and, but, or, so and because, and write compound sentences.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف طريقة حدوث الأشياء باستخدام الظروف، وأربط الأفكار بـ and وbut وor وso وbecause، وأكتب جملًا مركبة."});
